Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.31 auto-save: field idle hook

P6.31 Auto-save (docs/P6.31_AUTOSAVE.md). At the field's first idle frame (the
moment the field menu may open: no event, no menu, no fade, no banner), openFieldMenu
(field_mode/field.c) asks dw3_autosave_field_idle (port/autosave/autosave.c) with
FieldState's flags. With the Options screen's Auto-save row OFF (the default) the
call returns at once: nothing is read, written or logged, and the game runs as
without this patch. When the port answers "save now" (an area change, a slot the
player used, not in a battle) autosaveField builds the save the way
STGMCARD_fillSave does (the game's first GAME_SAVE_SIZE bytes, the XOR checksum
from byte 4, the region's version byte) but with the current mode, player
position and direction as the field menu would record them in GameState.fieldMode
/ fieldPos / fieldDir, in a private buffer: GAME itself is not changed. The
port writes it to the target slot (rename-atomic, rolled back on failure).

--- a/src/field/field_mode/field.c
+++ b/src/field/field_mode/field.c
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #if PORT_HOST
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include "overlay_host.h"
+#include "port_autosave.h"
 char *getenv(const char *name);
 long strtol(const char *nptr, char **endptr, int base);
 #ifdef DW3_CHEATS
@@ -559,6 +560,53 @@
  * From the story point 4 on, START opens the field menu (STSTATUS) while
  * the field is idle; the player's place is kept to come back to
  */
+#if PORT_HOST
+/* P6.31 auto-save: the field is idle on a new area, so write the game to the
+   slot the player used last. The save bytes are what STGMCARD_fillSave builds
+   (the game, its checksum from byte 4 and the region's version), with the
+   current area and the player's place as the field menu would record them
+   (GAME itself is not touched); the summary fields are the ones it fills for
+   the save list. port/autosave/autosave.c decides where and how it is written. */
+static void autosaveField(FieldChildren *children) {
+    static union {
+        u8 bytes[GAME_SAVE_SIZE];
+        GameState game;
+    } buf;
+    Dw3AutosaveSnapshot snap;
+    u8 sum = 0;
+    s32 i;
+    s32 member;
+
+    memcpy(buf.bytes, &GAME, GAME_SAVE_SIZE);
+    buf.game.fieldMode = GAME.funcs.getMode();
+    if (children->actors[0] != NULL) {
+        buf.game.fieldPos = children->actors[0]->pos;
+        buf.game.fieldDir = children->actors[0]->dir;
+    }
+    for (i = 4; i < GAME_SAVE_SIZE; i++) {
+        sum ^= buf.bytes[i];
+    }
+    buf.game.checksum = sum;
+#if VERSION_US
+    buf.game.version = 3;
+#elif VERSION_EU
+    buf.game.version = 4;
+#endif
+    snap.save = buf.bytes;
+    snap.save_size = GAME_SAVE_SIZE;
+    snap.mode = buf.game.fieldMode;
+    memcpy(snap.name, buf.game.name, sizeof(snap.name));
+    snap.money = buf.game.money;
+    memcpy(snap.play_time, &buf.game.playTime, sizeof(snap.play_time));
+    for (i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
+        member = GAME.funcs.getPartyMember(i);
+        snap.levels[i] = buf.game.partners[member].info.stats[STAT_LEVEL];
+        snap.partners[i] = buf.game.partners[member].unlocked;
+    }
+    dw3_autosave_commit(&snap);
+}
+#endif
